SAAS TIERED MONETIZATION & GATING TO-DO LIST

Phase 1: Core State & Permissions Framework
[ ] Define Global User State: Set up a lightweight user state object in app.js to track tiers ("guest", "registered", "paid").
[ ] Create Access Control Helper: Write a centralized checkAccess(requiredTier) function to evaluate if a user can perform an action or needs a prompt.

Phase 2: Table Row Limits (Data Gating)
[ ] Enforce Input Table Limits: Restrict data rows to 8 for Guests, 16 for Registered users, and Unlimited for Paid users.
[ ] Enforce Prediction Table Limits: Set corresponding row limits for the sample prediction table.
[ ] Add Row-Limit Triggers: Prevent the calculator from adding new input rows once the tier threshold is reached.

Phase 3: Model Gating ("Find Best Fit" & "Custom Model")
[ ] Update Model Dropdown UI: Add visual lock icons (🔒) next to restricted models for guests and free registered users.
[ ] Enforce Model Restrictions: Prevent guests and registered users from selecting "best_fit" or "custom", automatically redirecting them to standard models or triggering an upgrade prompt.

Phase 4: Copy & Export Permissions
[ ] Gate Copy Actions: Restrict copying equations, parameters, statistics, and predictions to Registered and Paid users (Guests are blocked with a signup prompt).
[ ] Gate Export Actions: Restrict data/report exports exclusively to Paid users.
[ ] Build Upgrade/Signup Modals: Replace standard browser alerts with a clean, friendly modal popup that invites users to log in or upgrade when they hit a locked feature.

Phase 5: Backend, Auth & Payments (Future Integration)
[ ] Integrate Authentication: Set up Supabase or Firebase Auth for secure email/password login and registration.
[ ] Integrate Stripe Checkout: Create a Pro subscription product in Stripe and link it to user accounts via webhooks to automatically upgrade user tiers upon successful payment.